# Domain and errors

## Domain purity
- Domain files import only dart: libraries, freezed_annotation, meta, lib/core/result and lib/core/error.
- No package:flutter, no Drift, no Dio, no get_it, no l10n.
- Entities are immutable freezed classes or sealed classes. Images are described with plain url and asset strings; presentation turns them into ImageRef.
- Validators are pure top-level functions or const classes in domain/validators with unit tests for every rule.
- Use cases are single classes with one call method and constructor-injected repositories.

## Result
- Every repository method returns Result<T> (or a stream of Result<T>). Use cases pass the Result through or combine with map, flatMap and fold.
- Never throw across the domain boundary. Never return null to mean failure.

## Failures
- AppFailure is sealed: StorageFailure, NetworkFailure, TimeoutFailure, NotFoundFailure, ValidationFailure, AuthFailure, UnexpectedFailure.
- Each failure carries a stable code, an optional cause and an optional stack trace.
- Data code throws AppException only internally; guardResult and guardStream convert every exception into an Err and log it with its stack trace.
- Every catch converts to Err, logs with the stack trace, or rethrows. Empty catches are forbidden.
- Presentation maps failures to localized text in one place: the AppFailure localization extension in lib/core/extensions.
